var e={"Testing RLS":`Testing RLS`,"Keep policy scenarios beside application migrations in `migrations/tests/`.\nRun them against a disposable `nelcota dev` database after applying your\nmigrations. The test process needs the local administrator connection to create\nfixtures and impersonate API roles. Never run these helpers against production.":"Keep policy scenarios beside application migrations in `migrations/tests/`.\nRun them against a disposable `nelcota dev` database after applying your\nmigrations. The test process needs the local administrator connection to create\nfixtures and impersonate API roles. Never run these helpers against production.","The `@nelcota/client/testing` export has no runtime dependencies and does not\nload the browser client. It supports a `pg.Pool` on Node or Bun and `Bun.SQL`.\nUse the source build containing this export until its SDK release is published.":"The `@nelcota/client/testing` export has no runtime dependencies and does not\nload the browser client. It supports a `pg.Pool` on Node or Bun and `Bun.SQL`.\nUse the source build containing this export until its SDK release is published.","Start a local scenario":`Start a local scenario`,"`DATABASE_URL` is the direct, URL-encoded local PostgreSQL connection. A test\nrunner may run scenarios in parallel only if each reserves its own connection\nand uses independent fixtures. Keep statements within one scenario sequential.":`\`DATABASE_URL\` is the direct, URL-encoded local PostgreSQL connection. A test
runner may run scenarios in parallel only if each reserves its own connection
and uses independent fixtures. Keep statements within one scenario sequential.`,"On Node, install `pg`, pass `new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL })`\nto the same helpers, and close the pool with `pool.end()` after the suite.\nNo driver is bundled or required by the ordinary SDK entry points.":"On Node, install `pg`, pass `new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL })`\nto the same helpers, and close the pool with `pool.end()` after the suite.\nNo driver is bundled or required by the ordinary SDK entry points.","Fixture contract":`Fixture contract`,"`openRollbackTransaction(pool)` returns `{ sql, rollback }`; always call\n`rollback()` in `finally`. Prefer `withRollbackTransaction(pool, scenario)`\nto make cleanup automatic. These helpers reserve one dedicated connection.":"`openRollbackTransaction(pool)` returns `{ sql, rollback }`; always call\n`rollback()` in `finally`. Prefer `withRollbackTransaction(pool, scenario)`\nto make cleanup automatic. These helpers reserve one dedicated connection.","`actAs(sql, 'authenticated', userId)` sets transaction-local role and JWT\nclaims, using the same `role`/`sub` format as the API. `actAsAnonymous(sql)`\nclears the previous subject. Both changes disappear on rollback.":"`actAs(sql, 'authenticated', userId)` sets transaction-local role and JWT\nclaims, using the same `role`/`sub` format as the API. `actAsAnonymous(sql)`\nclears the previous subject. Both changes disappear on rollback.","`createAuthUser(sql, { id?, email? })` creates a confirmed, passwordless\nfixture identity. It does not sign in or issue tokens; use the administrator\nfixture connection before impersonation.":`\`createAuthUser(sql, { id?, email? })\` creates a confirmed, passwordless
fixture identity. It does not sign in or issue tokens; use the administrator
fixture connection before impersonation.`,"`expectSqlState(sql, '42501', operation)` verifies a database rejection and\nrestores a savepoint. It accepts pg's `code` and Bun's `errno` SQLSTATE field,\nas described in [Bun's SQL error contract](https://bun.sh/docs/runtime/sql).":"`expectSqlState(sql, '42501', operation)` verifies a database rejection and\nrestores a savepoint. It accepts pg's `code` and Bun's `errno` SQLSTATE field,\nas described in [Bun's SQL error contract](https://bun.sh/docs/runtime/sql).","Do not issue `COMMIT` or change transaction ownership inside a scenario. Test\nRLS-hidden reads and writes as zero-row results as well as testing `WITH CHECK`\nfailures. Exercise two users, anonymous access and every permitted write verb.\nUse HTTP/SDK contract tests separately for JWT verification and route behavior.":"Do not issue `COMMIT` or change transaction ownership inside a scenario. Test\nRLS-hidden reads and writes as zero-row results as well as testing `WITH CHECK`\nfailures. Exercise two users, anonymous access and every permitted write verb.\nUse HTTP/SDK contract tests separately for JWT verification and route behavior."};export{e as default};